        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0327" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg251"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.51/1763</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Russell to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 106</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 24, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith
                    copies and translations of the answers to my two notes to the Council of
                    Ministers in regard to control of all the Dominican finances by the General
                    Receivership of Dominican Customs.</p>
                <p>In this connection I have to advise the Department that the General Receiver has
                    appointed Mr. J. H. Edwards to the new post of Controller and Disbursing Agent,
                    and he takes charge on Monday. The control commenced to be effective on the 16th
                    of this month, and no difficulty has been experienced so far in taking over the
                    various branches of the service in connection with this change.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">William W. Russell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d276-a1.xml" xpointer="d276-a1"/>
